// Brought to u by MidManStudio
//
// D1 v2, first step (chat 10): sema tags the result of a call to a user-defined @tier(mid) function that returns a struct or an
// enum with the arena the call is written in, so an arena value can no longer leave its block through such a call. 10 anchored
// edits over 5 files: crates/core/src/sema/type_infer.rs (the only code, which the other chat also moves, so it is edited and not
// replaced), docs/LLVM_POC.md, docs/LLVM_ROADMAP.md, docs/ARENA_BORROW_RULES.md and docs/LLVM_BACKEND_STATUS.md. Each anchor occurs exactly once on master
// and none starts at the beginning of a line.
//
// APPLY AFTER the tarball ubel-llvm-zmidref-18.tar.gz. The tarball makes the arena benchmark and fixture 55 lend their trees with
// `&`; without it they pass an arena value by value, and sema rejects that once this patch is in. The tarball also adds the
// fixtures that this patch turns from accepted to rejected, so apply the two together.
//
// This overwrites the earlier patch.mdix, which is right only because that one (the docs for stage 1, mine) is applied on master:
// check that first.

@CONFIG(
  version    -> "1.0.0",
  author     -> "MidManStudio",
  features   -> "quickfuncs,data",
  debug_mode -> "off"
)

@QUICKFUNCS(
  ~patch_replace_text<object>(_path, _anchor, _content) {
    return { path = _path, op = "replace_text", anchor = _anchor, content = _content }
  }
)

@DATA(
  patch_files::
    patch_replace_text("crates/core/src/sema/type_infer.rs", "return_type\n            }\n            SemaType::Var(_)   => self.fresh_var()", "self.tag_mid_call_result(callee, return_type)\n            }\n            SemaType::Var(_)   => self.fresh_var()")
    patch_replace_text("crates/core/src/sema/type_infer.rs", "inner:   inner_ty,\n            }),\n            None => inner_ty,\n        }\n    }", "inner:   inner_ty,\n            }),\n            None => inner_ty,\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// D1 v2, first step (provisional, decision D10): the result of a call to a user-defined `@tier(mid)` function that\n    /// returns a struct or an enum is built in the caller's arena (the native backend hands such a function the arena of its\n    /// caller), so a call written inside `with arena` is tagged like a freshly built value, as the result of a method call\n    /// already is. Without this the result of such a call passes every escape check. An optional or a list of such values\n    /// is not covered yet.\n    fn tag_mid_call_result<'ast>(&mut self, callee: &Expr<'ast>, result: TypeId) -> TypeId {\n        let Some(def) = self.callee_fn_def(callee) else { return result };\n        if !matches!(self.ctx.symbols.lookup(def).kind, DefKind::Function { tier: TierAnnotation::Mid, .. }) {\n            return result;\n        }\n        let resolved = self.apply(result);\n        let holds_object = match self.ctx.types.get(resolved).clone() {\n            SemaType::Named { def, .. } => matches!(self.ctx.symbols.lookup(def).kind, DefKind::Struct { .. } | DefKind::Enum),\n            _ => false,\n        };\n        if holds_object { self.maybe_arena_ref(result) } else { result }\n    }")
    patch_replace_text("docs/LLVM_POC.md", "**Known hole (D1 v2).** Sema does not tag the result of a call to such a function, so an arena value can leave its block through one.", "**D1 v2, first step: the escape hole is closed (decision D10, provisional).** Sema now tags the result of a call to such a function with the arena the call is written in, as it already did for the result of a method call, so an arena value can no longer leave its block through one.")
    patch_replace_text("docs/LLVM_POC.md", "is accepted; the same escape written as a struct literal in the block is rejected (TIER-004).", "was accepted before this step and is now rejected (TIER-004), as the same escape written as a struct literal in the block always was.")
    patch_replace_text("docs/LLVM_POC.md", "The accepted program reads an arena that has been destroyed (it printed the expected number in a test, which proves nothing). Closing it is D1 v2: tag the result with the region of the arena the call was given. Until then it is a gap that only programs that did not compile before can reach.", "Because a struct has reference semantics, such a result crosses a call only as a borrow: a tree built by `make` is lent with `&` (`check(&t)`, which the native backend now allows for enums as well as structs), not passed by value. Not covered yet: a function that returns an optional or a list of such values.")
    patch_replace_text("docs/LLVM_POC.md", "- 2026-11-25 (chat 10): **Stage 1 of D10:", "- 2026-11-26 (chat 10): **D1 v2, first step: sema tags the result of a MID call, and the native backend lends enums.** The owner chose D1 v2 and then, shown that tagging makes passing an arena value by value (`check(make(depth))`) a sema error, chose that callees must borrow with `&T`. Two deliveries, in this order: the tarball ubel-llvm-zmidref-18 (`emit.rs`: a reference to an enum is the enum's own pointer, as for a struct, both as the type `&Enum` and as the expression `&e`; the arena benchmark and fixture 55 lend with `&`; fixture 60; five core fixtures) and then this patch (`type_infer.rs`: `tag_mid_call_result`, 2 edits). Effect: the escape reproduced in the stage-1 entry is rejected with TIER-004, and a call to a user-defined `@tier(mid)` function that returns a struct or an enum, written inside `with arena`, is tagged with that block's arena. Fixtures: `err_arena_mid_result_escape`, `_enum_escape`, `_by_value`, `ok_arena_mid_result_borrow`, `ok_arena_low_result_untagged` (the three `err_` ones are accepted until this patch is applied). Verified on fresh clones of master 57e931a, first with the tarball alone and then with the patch: with the tarball alone: ubel_llvm 6 unit and 19 integration tests, `run_equiv.sh` 139 passed and 0 failed, `run_ubel_build.sh` 74 supported programs equal to `ubel run` and 58 intentional refusals, and only the three new `err_` fixtures reported as accepted (they need this patch); with the tarball and this patch: core lib 232, ubel_llvm 6 unit and 19 integration, the CLI suites and doc-tests ok, `run_equiv.sh` 139 passed and 0 failed at 64-bit and with `-m32`, `run_ubel_build.sh` 74 supported programs equal to `ubel run`, 58 intentional refusals, 217 `err_` rejected, 33 of 203 `ok_` built (32 of 201 before: the new `ok_arena_mid_result_borrow` builds and the new `ok_arena_low_result_untagged` is refused for LOW); GC stress 1 with ASan and UBSan on fixtures 55 to 60, the borrowing benchmark and the list, optional and arena-scan examples; langbench `--size small` correct for every installed language, ubel-mid included. A prototype of the tagging changed no `ok_` or `err_` fixture and no example program outside the fixtures. Mutation testing by hand: 7 mutants of the new code, all caught: the enum reference type and the enum borrow refused again (fixture 55), the tagging hook removed, enums only, structs only, and every result tagged (the three `err_` fixtures and fixture 57), and the MID-only check removed, which survived until `ok_arena_low_result_untagged` was added (MID may call LOW, and a LOW result is not arena memory). Not covered: a MID function that returns an optional or a list of such values (`Node?`) is still untagged; HIGH code cannot reach these functions. Not verified: the hosted runner, ARM, macOS, Termux.\n- 2026-11-25 (chat 10): **Stage 1 of D10:")
    patch_replace_text("docs/LLVM_ROADMAP.md", "Known hole: sema does not tag the result of a call to such a function (D1 v2), so an arena value can escape its block through one (docs/LLVM_POC.md, Tier lowering).", "Hole closed in chat 10 (D1 v2, first step): sema tags the result of a call to such a function with the arena the call is written in, so an arena value crosses a call only as a borrow (`check(&t)`); optional and list results are not covered yet.")
    patch_replace_text("docs/ARENA_BORROW_RULES.md", "- **Region-polymorphic results** (`pick` above) are refused.", "- **Results of a `@tier(mid)` call (D1 v2, first step, provisional).** The result of a call to a user-defined `@tier(mid)` function that returns a struct or an enum is built in the caller's arena, so a call written inside `with arena` is tagged with that block's arena like a freshly built value (the result of a method call already was). It then follows the rules above: it can be lent with `&` and read, but not kept outside the block, returned from it, or passed by value. Fixtures: `err_arena_mid_result_escape`, `err_arena_mid_result_enum_escape`, `err_arena_mid_result_by_value`, `ok_arena_mid_result_borrow`, and `ok_arena_low_result_untagged` (the result of a `@tier(low)` call is not arena memory and is not tagged). An optional or a list of such values is not covered yet.\n- **Region-polymorphic results** (`pick` above) are refused.")
    patch_replace_text("docs/LLVM_BACKEND_STATUS.md", "references to anything but a struct, qualified type names", "references to anything but a struct or an enum, qualified type names")
    patch_replace_text("docs/LLVM_POC.md", "a reference to anything but a struct (`&L int`)", "a reference to anything but a struct or an enum (`&L int`)")
)
